        "Leprosy is diagnosed by any one of an anaesthetic hypopigmented patch, a thickened nerve with sensory or motor loss, or a positive slit-skin smear; it is paucibacillary with up to five patches and multibacillary beyond that, treated free with rifampicin, clofazimine and dapsone for six or twelve months, and the patient is told in advance about orange urine, skin darkening and anaemia.",
